- op: discuss  # 7d15
  at: '2026-09-15T21:29:10Z'  # 7d15
  by: agent  # 7d15
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7d15
  clock: 3  # 7d15
  nonce: 7d15  # 7d15
  message: "GOVERNANCE APPROVAL REQUESTED -- comment text only, no PR opened.\n\nTHE ASK. Correct five comment sites in `scripts/auto-pr` (lines 1085, 1494,\n2326) and `.githooks/reference-transaction` (lines 22 and 35). No behaviour\nchanges, no new tests. Both files are governance, so even a comment diff waits\non your word.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT HOUSEKEEPING. These comments say the recover marker covers \"fetch\n+ post-merge fast-forward\". It covers the whole run, CI poll included -- up to\n~45 minutes for auto-pr and up to its `ci_timeout` for do_sync. WI-pohir then\nproposed detecting a leaked marker by age, reasoning that \"no auto-pr fetch+ff\nwindow is that long\". That is a faithful reading of these comments, and shipped\nas written it would have false-alarmed on every auto-pr with slow CI. I caught\nit only because I measured the span instead of reading it, and that is not\nsomething to depend on a second time.\n\nTHE SMALLER HALF. reference-transaction:22 still sends an operator to a manual\n`tracker recover` for the clean/stash gap. AGENTS.md now sends them to\n`reconcile`, because `recover` restores the journal and leaves the repo behind\nthe upstream -- which is exactly how the other two steps get skipped.\n\nDELIBERATELY SEPARATE FROM WI-gokuv, which touches the same two files. WI-gokuv\nmay end up `wont_do` if its fd-inheritance premise fails under test; these\ncomments should be corrected either way, and I do not want one to hold the other\nhostage.\n\nALREADY DONE WITHOUT WAITING: the tracker-package half of the same\nmis-description -- `cli.py` and `test_reconcile.py`, both saying \"around its own\nfetch\" -- is not governance and is being corrected now."  # 7d15
- op: discuss  # c308
  at: '2026-09-15T22:25:17Z'  # c308
  by: agent  # c308
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c308
  clock: 4  # c308
  nonce: c308  # c308
  message: "FOLDED INTO PR #977 (WI-gokuv), and I am reversing my own \"keep them separate\"\ndecision on the record rather than quietly.\n\nI argued for separation because WI-gokuv might end up wont_do if its\nfd-inheritance premise failed, and these comments deserved correcting either\nway. The premise was tested and held, the owner said to tackle WI-gokuv, and at\nthat point the separation stopped making sense: the conversion REWRITES the very\nlines this item is about. Keeping them apart would have meant writing the\nalready-known-wrong comment once more, then correcting it in the next PR.\n\nAll five sites this item names are corrected in #977:\n  * scripts/auto-pr 1085 / 1494 / 2326 -- the three \"fetch + post-merge\n    fast-forward\" comments are gone; those sites now call\n    _autopr_hold_recover_lock, whose header states the span is the WHOLE action\n    including the CI poll, names the 2400s + 300s numbers, and says outright\n    that the old wording is how WI-pohir came to believe fifteen minutes was a\n    safe bound.\n  * .githooks/reference-transaction:35 -- same correction, plus the reason the\n    guard is now a lock test rather than a file test.\n  * .githooks/reference-transaction:22 -- the clean/stash gap now points at\n    `tracker reconcile`, and says explicitly that `recover` is the deprecated\n    journal-only half that leaves the repo behind the upstream.\n\nThe non-governance half (cli.py, test_reconcile.py) shipped separately in PR\n#975 as planned.\n\nClosing this when #977 merges, not before: the correction only exists on a\nbranch until then."  # c308
